  "query_preview": "..The upper air pattern is transitioning over\nArizona at the moment as a trough moves from Chihuahua into \nwest Texas and ridging builds in behind it. At the surface winds\nremain easterly, but not as strong as over the weekend with \nspeeds generally 8-12 mph. Tuesday into Thursday the \naforementioned ridge will dominate Arizona leading to a small \nwarmup compared to this past weekend. High temperatures will be \naround normal to a couple degrees above normal. \n\nFriday into early next week the upper air pattern becomes more \nprogressive as ensembles show a couple troughs moving through. \nThe first low pinches off from the main longwave trough over the\nGulf of Alaska and moves through Baja into Sonora Friday into \nSaturday. This is a little further south than past model runs \nwith still some uncertainty on the exact track. However both \nthe GEFS and Euro ensemble increase moisture as the low moves \nthrough bringing rain chances to Arizona Friday evening into \nSaturday. Still lots of differences in how the second trough \ndevelops and tracks, but will follow the cutoff low moving \nthrough the region starting either Sunday or Monday into early \nnext week. This will keep rain chances in the forecast Sunday \nand Monday. Temperatures will also cool to a few degrees below \nnormal this weekend.",
